  {"name": "West checkstand bank, lane interiors (audit 2026-07-27) — the register/belt/bagging assemblies from x=386 to x=550, y 584-623. Store 92 draws its lanes as ~4 pt gaps that are open at BOTH ends, so no enclosed pocket ever forms behind them and the derived auto:CHECKSTANDS zone (rect 343,521-756,631, bridge 20) has nothing to cull: the bank shipped fully green, and the shortest path from the front action alley to the post-checkout strip ran straight down a 0.43 m lane at x=665 (geodesic/euclid 1.04, against 1.95-6.60 on every other onboarded store; baseline 659 renders its bank solid white). 20 columns crossed the bank end to end. A checkout lane is not a corridor the router may thread mid-trip, so it is excluded like any other drawn-open-but-unusable floor. The rect stops at x=552 and starts at x=384, leaving the Ice-box/Tobacco walkway (x 552-626) and the bank's west approach (x 368-384) open, which is how a shopper actually gets from the alley to the Exit.",
